ions that might need adjustments, but I’m not entirely sure. Let me know your thoughts when you can.\"*  \n\n*After (3-Sentence Rule):*  \n*\"Hi [Name], I’d appreciate your feedback on the report I sent last week. Specifically, could you review Sections 3 and 4 for accuracy? Please share your edits by Wednesday.\"*  \n\n**References**  \n- *Harvard Business Review*: \"How to Write Email with Military Precision\"  \n- *The Brief Lab*: Techniques for concise business communication.  \n\n**Practice Exercise**  \nRewrite the following message using the 3-sentence rule:  \n*\"Hey, just checking in to see if you got my previous email about the meeting reschedule. I think we need to move it to Thursday because of the client conflict, but I’m not sure if that works for everyone. Maybe you could ask the team?\"*  \n\nFocus on cutting fluff and structuring the request clearly."
